{"id": "BT-0051", "category": "recon", "issue": "BT-0051 duplicates BT-0050: same supplier invoice and amount, entered twice, with no bank statement line behind the second entry.", "proposed_fix": "Delete or void BT-0051 (Reece Plumbing Supply, $1,848.00). Keep BT-0050, which is reconciled to SL-0050. This takes $1,848.00 of spend off the Xero bank account and $168.00 of GST credit off the claim.", "evidence": "BT-0050: SPEND, 2026-08-11, Reece Plumbing Supply, Reference \"INV 88412\", \"Materials, job J-121\", acct 310, INPUT, LineAmount 1680.00, Tax 168.00, Total 1848.00, IsReconciled true, matched to SL-0050 (2026-08-11, REECE PLUMBING SUPPLY, -1848.00). BT-0051: SPEND, 2026-08-12, Reece Plumbing Supply, Reference \"88412\", \"Materials, J-121\", acct 310, INPUT, LineAmount 1680.00, Tax 168.00, Total 1848.00, IsReconciled false. No statement line is matched to BT-0051, and no other -1848.00 line appears on the August statement.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:33"}
{"id": "BT-0046", "category": "coding", "issue": "A laptop costing more than the $1,000 capitalise threshold was expensed to Repairs and Maintenance instead of being capitalised.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the line from 473 Repairs and Maintenance to 720 Computer Equipment (fixed asset), $2,635.45 ex GST (GST $263.55 unchanged), and add it to the asset register for depreciation.", "evidence": "BT-0046, 2026-08-16, Contact JB Hi-Fi Business (default account 720), Description \"Laptop for estimator\", AccountCode 473, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 2635.45, TaxAmount 263.55, Total 2899.00. Org policy CapitaliseThreshold 1000.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:33"}
{"id": "BT-0047", "category": "coding", "issue": "A joinery installation by a subcontractor was coded to Materials instead of Subcontractors.", "proposed_fix": "Recode the line from 310 Materials to 315 Subcontractors, $5,800.00 ex GST (GST $580.00 unchanged).", "evidence": "BT-0047, 2026-08-22, Contact Pinewood Joinery (default account 315; its other August payments BT-0030, BT-0031 and BT-0033 are coded 315), Description \"Joinery install, job J-118\", AccountCode 310, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 5800.00, TaxAmount 580.00, Total 6380.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:35"}
{"id": "BT-0052", "category": "recon", "issue": "BT-0052 is recorded in Xero at $1,254.00, but the bank statement line it is reconciled to (SL-0051) shows $1,524.00, which looks like a digit transposition.", "proposed_fix": "Change BT-0052 to the bank amount of $1,524.00 (GST-inclusive: LineAmount 1385.45, Tax 138.55 at 1/11), then re-reconcile it to SL-0051. First check the figure against the Coastal Electrical Contractors invoice for the J-124 progress claim. If the invoice is $1,254.00, the extra $270.00 was overpaid and needs to go to the client as a question.", "evidence": "SL-0051: 2026-08-24, COASTAL ELECTRICAL CON, Amount -1524.00, MatchedTransactionID BT-0052. BT-0052: SPEND, 2026-08-24, Coastal Electrical Contractors, \"Progress claim, job J-124\", acct 315, INPUT, LineAmount 1140.00, Tax 114.00, Total 1254.00, IsReconciled true. Difference: 270.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:36"}
{"id": "BT-0048", "category": "coding", "issue": "A Woolworths grocery purchase was coded to Entertainment, but it looks like private spending by the owner.", "proposed_fix": "Unless the client can show a business purpose, recode the full $214.35 to 880 Owner A Drawings (BASEXCLUDED, so no GST credit). Question for the client: were these groceries for the business, such as staff amenities or a site event, or were they personal?", "evidence": "BT-0048, 2026-08-23, Contact Woolworths, Description \"Groceries\", AccountCode 420 Entertainment, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 194.86, TaxAmount 19.49, Total 214.35. No reference or job number.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:38"}
{"id": "BT-0043", "category": "gst", "issue": "A GST credit of $360.00 was claimed on a payment to a supplier that is not registered for GST.", "proposed_fix": "Change the tax rate from INPUT to GST Free Expenses (no GST). The line becomes $3,960.00 with $0.00 GST, and the $360.00 GST credit comes off the BAS. Account 315 stays the same.", "evidence": "BT-0043, 2026-08-26, SPEND, Contact Ridge Tiling (sole trader) (C006, ABN 71 824 330 016, IsGSTRegistered=false); line 'Tiling, job J-121', AccountCode 315, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 3600.00, TaxAmount 360.00, Total 3960.00.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:39"}
{"id": "SL-0052", "category": "recon", "issue": "Statement line SL-0052, an $8,420.00 ATO payment on 28 Aug 2026, has no matching transaction in Xero.", "proposed_fix": "Create a $8,420.00 spend transaction dated 2026-08-28 to ATO, tax type BAS Excluded, and reconcile it to SL-0052. Where it should be coded depends on what the payment was for. Question for the client: which period and which liability does this payment cover (for example the July or quarterly BAS/IAS, PAYG withholding, GST, or income tax instalment), so it can be coded to the right ATO liability or ATO clearing account?", "evidence": "SL-0052: 2026-08-28, Payee \"ATO PAYMENT\", Amount -8420.00, MatchedTransactionID null. No Xero bank transaction for the period has contact ATO or a total of 8420.00.", "confidence": "medium", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:40"}
{"id": "BT-0049", "category": "coding", "issue": "A 12-month insurance premium running to 31 Jul 2027 was expensed in full in August instead of being treated as a prepayment.", "proposed_fix": "Code the $4,800.00 ex GST to 620 Prepayments, then release $400.00 a month to 433 Insurance. For August this means 433 shows $400.00 and 620 carries $4,400.00 at 31 Aug 2026. GST of $480.00 is unchanged.", "evidence": "BT-0049, 2026-08-02, Contact QBE Insurance, Description \"Contract works insurance, 12 months to 31 Jul 2027\", AccountCode 433, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 4800.00, TaxAmount 480.00, Total 5280.00. Cover period is 1 Aug 2026 to 31 Jul 2027, which is 12 months at $400.00 a month.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:41"}
{"id": "BT-0044", "category": "gst", "issue": "Casual wages were coded with GST on Expenses, which claims a $300.00 GST credit on wages even though wages carry no GST.", "proposed_fix": "Change the tax rate from INPUT to BAS Excluded. The line becomes $3,300.00 with $0.00 GST, and the $300.00 GST credit is removed.", "evidence": "BT-0044, 2026-08-17, SPEND, Contact Payroll Clearing (C020, no ABN, IsGSTRegistered=false); line 'Weekly wages (casual)', AccountCode 477 (default tax BASEXCLUDED), TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 3000.00, TaxAmount 300.00, Total 3300.00. The other wage runs (BT-0001 to BT-0005) are coded BASEXCLUDED with $0 GST.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:42"}
{"id": "BT-0045", "category": "gst", "issue": "The GST amount is wrong: $217.80 is 11.1% of the net amount, not 1/11 of the $2,178.00 total, so GST is overclaimed by $19.80.", "proposed_fix": "Recalculate with GST as 1/11 of the total. GST is $198.00 and the net line amount is $1,980.00 (total stays $2,178.00). This reduces the GST credit by $19.80.", "evidence": "BT-0045, 2026-08-09, SPEND, Contact Laminex Direct (IsGSTRegistered=true); line 'Benchtop laminate, job J-124', AccountCode 310, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 1960.20, TaxAmount 217.80, Total 2178.00. 2178.00/11 = 198.00; 1960.20 x 10% = 196.02, which is also not equal to 217.80.", "confidence": "high", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:45"}
{"id": "BT-0048", "category": "gst", "issue": "A full GST credit was claimed on a Woolworths groceries purchase coded to Entertainment, where the GST credit is probably not claimable.", "proposed_fix": "Question for the client: what were these groceries for (staff or client entertainment, site amenities, or private)? If entertainment or private, change the tax rate to GST on Expenses non-claimable or BAS Excluded, with $0.00 GST on $214.35, which removes the $19.49 credit. If they were for business amenities, claim GST only on the taxable items shown on the receipt, because basic food is GST free.", "evidence": "BT-0048, 2026-08-23, SPEND, Contact Woolworths (C018, IsGSTRegistered=true); line 'Groceries', AccountCode 420 Entertainment, TaxType INPUT, LineAmount 194.86, TaxAmount 19.49, Total 214.35. No receipt breakdown available.", "confidence": "low", "queued_at": "2026-09-29T12:53:48"}

